    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, i manage a rental property in phoenix and one of the tenants is complaining that the ac is running all the time but her master bedroom stays really hot compared to the rest of the house. what are some common reasons this happens?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Common reasons for the master bedroom to remain hot while other areas stay cool could include thermal leaks, fewer conditioned air outlets (like vents or registers), improper AC sizing, or blocked air flow. It may also be due to the placement of curtains or blinds, as they can trap heat inside. It might also be helpful to ask the tenant to check if the AC vents in her room are closed or blocked and ensure the AC filter is clean. If these simple fixes don't help, you might need to consider having a professional HVAC technician inspect the system for faults.",
