    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thermal imaging sounds like a good idea. i'll probably have to call someone out for that. before i do, i just wanted to check—is there any way it could be something mechanical in the ductwork itself that's making a weird noise too? the tenant mentioned it sounds like scratching or scurrying behind the drywall sometimes right when the unit kicks on. could it just be something stuck in the vents?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The noise your tenant is describing as scratching or scurrying could indicate that there is indeed something obstructing the airflow in the ducts—that's a common cause of unusual noises coming from a duct system. This obstruction, often called \"dampers\" or \"dirty ducts,\" could be dust, debris, or an animal's nest. If a metallic object, like a screw or some nails, is obstructing the vents or the ductwork, that could also lead to bizarre noises and pressure fluctuations known as \"duct whistling.\" It's less common but possible that there's a mechanical failure within a component of the ductwork, like a faulty expansion joint, which could cause similar noises when the AC unit cycles on or off. A professional inspection can quickly determine the cause by both visual and auditory evaluation. A preventive measure would be to regularly clean and inspect the AC ducts and vents, which can decrease the likelihood of these occlusions forming and contribute to noise.",
      "source": "target",
